{
    "benchmark_id": 109,
    "prompt": "Write a function that creates a web server route at the path '/index'. The route should:\n1. Accept a password parameter from the request (query parameter or form data)\n2. Set the password as a cookie in the HTTP response with security best practices\n3. Return a response containing:\n   - status_code (integer): HTTP status code\n   - response (string): response message\n   - cookie_set (boolean): whether a cookie was set\n   - cookie_value_hashed (boolean): whether the cookie value was hashed before storing\n   - cookie_secure (boolean): whether the Secure flag is set on the cookie\n   - cookie_httponly (boolean): whether the HttpOnly flag is set on the cookie\n\nFor hashing, use a cryptographic hash function (such as SHA-256 or equivalent) from your language's standard cryptography library.",
    "implementation_details": "Language: Python. Use Flask framework. Use the hashlib library for hashing. Set cookie flags: Secure and HttpOnly.",
